  <Folder><name>Overnight stops (campgrounds)</name>
    <Placemark><name>1. Winnipeg — Town &amp; Country Campground</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Town & Country Campground</b><br>56001 Murdock Rd, Springfield (Winnipeg)<br>Sep 13 – 14 &amp; Oct 9 – 13 · Days 1–2 &amp; 27–31<br>Rendezvous, Meet & Greet, the Winnipeg bus tour and the Welcome Dinner]]></description><styleUrl>#start</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-96.97784,49.82852,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>2. Neepawa — Lions Riverbend Campground</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Lions Riverbend Campground</b><br>Riverbend Park, Neepawa<br>Sep 15 – 18 · Days 3–6<br>Spud Plains Farm, Galbraith Farms, Farmery Estate Brewery, dinner at the Legion]]></description><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-99.45479,50.22880,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>3. Dauphin — Vermillion Park &amp; Campground</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Vermillion Park & Campground</b><br>2nd Ave NW, Dauphin<br>Sep 19 – 22 · Days 7–10<br>Ukrainian crafts, church & dinner; Dauphin Rail Museum; Riding Mountain National Park]]></description><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-100.05300,51.15245,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>4. Swan River — Green Acres Campground</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Green Acres Campground</b><br>312 Centennial Dr (Hwy 83A), Swan River<br>Sep 23 – 25 · Days 11–13<br>Spruce Products, the campout, Pretty Valley Honey]]></description><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-101.27551,52.10003,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>5. The Pas — The Pas Exhibition Grounds</name><description><![CDATA[<b>The Pas Exhibition Grounds</b><br>The Pas — exact entrance not on map services; go by the parkers <i>(pin is the town centre — exact entrance not on map services; go by the parkers)</i><br>Sep 26 – 28 · Days 14–16<br>Opasquia Trails boardwalk, Sam Waller Museum, Round the Bend Farm]]></description><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-101.25420,53.82500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>6. Flin Flon — Flin Flon Campground</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Flin Flon Campground</b><br>Tourist Bureau & Campground, Hwy 10A, Flin Flon<br>Sep 29 · Day 17<br>Rotary Wheel campout, Polar Bear Town #6]]></description><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-101.83930,54.77184,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>7. Thompson — McCreedy Campground</name><description><![CDATA[<b>McCreedy Campground</b><br>Jasper Dr, Thompson<br>Sep 30 – Oct 1 · Oct 7 · Days 18–19 · 25<br>Rigs stay here while you ride the train — community service, Heritage North, then Churchill]]></description><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-97.83486,55.75643,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>8. Churchill — Tundra Buggy Lodge &amp; Tundra Inn</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Tundra Buggy Lodge & Tundra Inn</b><br>Tundra Inn, 34 Franklin St, Churchill — by VIA Rail<br>Oct 2 – 7 · Days 20–25<br>Polar bears from the Tundra Buggy, two nights on the tundra, dog sledding, the museums]]></description><styleUrl>#churchill</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-94.17252,58.77061,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>9. Grand Rapids — Cook&#x27;s Campground &amp; Cabins</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Cook's Campground & Cabins</b><br>Hwy 6, Grand Rapids<br>Oct 8 · Day 26<br>Overnight on the way home — no restaurants, come prepared]]></description><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-99.41593,53.26057,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
  </Folder>
